ality is universally valued in principle, living it out authentically is a complex, lifelong endeavor. And they agreed that whether one sees that journey through the lens of karma or humanistic ethics, the effort to continually align one\u2019s actions with one\u2019s values is what truly matters.\n\nThis dialogue illustrates that regardless of belief systems, the challenge of living a moral life is one that resonates deeply, prompting both reflection and a shared desire for personal growth."}
