eligious backgrounds might be influencing their perspectives.\n\u2003\u2022 It could also be valuable to explore a variety of teaching strategies that acknowledge and respect different worldviews while still meeting educational goals.\n\u2003\u2022 Professional development or collaboration with colleagues on culturally responsive teaching methods can help educators better understand and support the diverse needs of their students.\n\nIn summary, while religious and cultural backgrounds can influence students\u2019 attitudes toward science, the differences observed in the classroom are likely the result of a complex interplay of factors. A sensitive, open-minded approach that seeks to understand each student\u2019s individual experience will be most effective in addressing any disparities in engagement."}
